      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays' offense has gone into a coma, scoring just two runs across 26 innings in Seattle before <strong>being shut out 4-0 by the Mariners on Sunday</strong>. That loss capped a disastrous weekend where they fell 11-0 the night before, dropping to 42-48 and sitting 3rd in the AL East, 11.5 games behind the division leader. The wRC+ has dipped to 93 - 22nd in baseball, the first time since 2019 the lineup has been below league average. Trey Yesavage threw a quality start but was undone by bats that couldn't find a rhythm, while Vladimir Guerrero Jr. managed only a single double in the final game. The bullpen held, but the team is now on a 2-game losing streak and the pressure is mounting. <strong>Tonight, they fly to San Francisco to face the Giants at 9:45 PM ET, hoping to break the slump before the All-Star break looms.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 6, 2026"
      },
